# grade: Π, rejecting: a finding refutes that the definition shows the rule's condition, as written; silence affirms nothing.
# Rule 1: a function returns a value, never a reference (read through any
# alias: the canonical return type).  const T and
# const T& are one value only while no reference into an argument escapes;
# the translation into System F erases references and cannot see a dangling
# one.  Exempt: the standard iterator protocol (a nested iterator or
# sentinel, by exact name), which Rule 3's folds run on.  Blind spot: decltype(auto) in a
# template pattern is undeduced and not seen.
#
# Sugar, a const accessor (#1223): a const member function returning const T&
# whose every return gives a field of its own object, or an element of one
# (a[i] on a built-in array or by operator[]), reached from this alone,
# implicitly or written, through fields only, is read as returning that
# field or element by value.  The reference is to the object's own storage,
# which lives as long as the object it was called on and cannot change under
# a const function, so nothing tells it from a copy.  Not exempt, and still
# refused: a reference to a parameter, a local, a static, a temporary (a
# field of a call's result), a non-const member function, a function that is
# not a member, a mutable reference.  Three conditions close what the reading
# would change: no field on the path is mutable (rule1-local-state refuses
# such a return, there being no matcher for a mutable field); no reference
# local is bound to the reference a call returns (rule1-local-state too: on a
# temporary, make_box().get() dangles in C++ and not in the reading); and the
# result's type is not observed by decltype or a type trait, which the author
# holds (std::is_reference_v gives true in C++, false in the reading).
# Fixtures: sugar-conditions.cpp, local-state.cpp.
let selfref expr(anyOf(cxxThisExpr(),
    memberExpr(member(fieldDecl()), unless(hasObjectExpression(unless(cxxThisExpr()))))))
let own memberExpr(member(fieldDecl()), unless(hasObjectExpression(unless(selfref))))
let ownelement expr(anyOf(own,
    arraySubscriptExpr(hasBase(ignoringParenImpCasts(own))),
    cxxOperatorCallExpr(hasOverloadedOperatorName("[]"), hasArgument(0, ignoringParenImpCasts(own)))))
let accessor cxxMethodDecl(isConst(), returns(hasCanonicalType(references(qualType(isConstQualified())))),
    hasBody(stmt(hasDescendant(returnStmt()),
        unless(hasDescendant(returnStmt(unless(hasReturnValue(ignoringParenImpCasts(ownelement)))))))))
match functionDecl(isExpansionInMainFile(), returns(hasCanonicalType(referenceType())), unless(anyOf(isImplicit(), isDefaulted(), isDeleted(), accessor, cxxMethodDecl(ofClass(cxxRecordDecl(isLambda()))), cxxMethodDecl(ofClass(cxxRecordDecl(matchesName("::(const_)?iterator$|::sentinel$")))))), hasAncestor(scope))
